The (Directive (EU) 2019/882) entered into application on 28 June 2025, harmonising accessibility requirements for a range of digital products and services sold within the , including e-commerce, banking, e-books, transport, and telecommunications. Although the United Kingdom left the European Union before the deadline, the directive continues to apply to UK businesses that supply covered products or services to EU consumers, irrespective of the supplier’s country of establishment. Microenterprises with fewer than 10 employees and an annual turnover below €2 million are exempt from some of the requirements.The European Accessibility ActEuropean Accessibility Act (Directive (EU) 2019/882) entered into application on 28 June 2025, harmonising accessibility requirements for a range of digital products and services sold within the European UnionEuropean Union, including e-commerce, banking, e-books, transport, and telecommunications.
